    "text": "Aithirne, also Aitherne, was an Irish poet and hero, called the Importunate. He abused the rule that no poet could be refused. His greed was great; he mocked any man or thing, even a river, that did not feed him. A bridge of saplings was built over the River Liffey so he could drive his sheep. He said he would sleep with the wife of the king of Ulster. When she refused, his satire killed her. The men of Ulster set his house on fire.",
